# Bus Reservation System (PS 19)

Console bus reservation application in Java.

## Problem
Search buses by destination, book and cancel tickets, and sort buses by fare. If a bus is full, the passenger joins that bus's waiting queue and gets the seat automatically when a ticket is cancelled.

## Concepts used
| Concept | Where |
|---|---|
| ArrayList | `buses` (all buses), `Bus.booked` (tickets) |
| Queue | `Bus.waiting` (`LinkedList` as FIFO queue, one per bus) |
| Searching | `findBus()` and `searchByDestination()` (linear search) |
| Sorting | `sortByFare()` (bubble sort on a copy of the list) |
| Methods | one method per feature |
| File handling | `loadData()` at start, `saveData()` on exit |

## Run
```
javac Main.java
java Main
```
Keep `buses.txt` in the same folder.

## Menu
1. View buses  2. Search by destination  3. Book ticket  4. Cancel ticket  5. Sort by fare  6. Exit (saves)

## Data file (`buses.txt`)
```
B101,Raipur-Bhopal,700,2
B102,Raipur-Nagpur,450,2
```
On exit the program saves the full state back to the same file: booked tickets, waiting queues and the next ticket number (`#next=`). To reset to the original data, restore the two lines above.

## Test cases (run on fresh data, one session)
| # | Input | Output |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Option 3, B101, Riya | Ticket booked. TKT101 \| Riya \| B101 Raipur-Bhopal, Seats left: 1 |
| 2 | Option 3, B101, Aman | Ticket booked. TKT102 \| Aman \| B101 Raipur-Bhopal, Seats left: 0 |
| 3 | Option 3, B999 | Bus B999 not found. |
| 4a | Option 3, B101, Dev | Bus full. Dev added to waiting queue. |
| 4b | Option 4, TKT101 | Ticket TKT101 cancelled. Seat given to Dev: TKT103 |
| 4c | Option 5 | B102 \| 450, B101 \| 700 |

## Validation handled
Unknown bus ID, unknown ticket ID, empty passenger name, invalid menu option, missing data file.